WEBVTT

00:00:00.300 --> 00:00:02.688
Let’s walk through Your specialist boundary.

00:00:02.688 --> 00:00:05.963
Confirm the queue and decision boundary assigned to this specialist

00:00:05.963 --> 00:00:06.862
seat.

00:00:06.862 --> 00:00:09.475
Visibility does not mean an item is ready, and

00:00:09.475 --> 00:00:13.262
no other operator may approve, override, return,

00:00:13.262 --> 00:00:15.738
copy, or acknowledge on your behalf.

00:00:15.738 --> 00:00:19.400
On this slide, as Diplomacy & Information SME,

00:00:19.400 --> 00:00:22.438
you own only the review or external handoff assigned to

00:00:22.438 --> 00:00:23.337
this seat.

00:00:23.885 --> 00:00:27.148
In practice, use the persisted source evidence, record

00:00:27.148 --> 00:00:31.635
each outcome explicitly, and leave deterministic exercise decisions

00:00:31.635 --> 00:00:33.398
with their owning workflow.

00:00:33.398 --> 00:00:36.185
Before you continue, verify these points:

00:00:36.185 --> 00:00:38.472
Work only the active session queue.

00:00:38.472 --> 00:00:40.597
Do not infer missing evidence.

00:00:40.597 --> 00:00:44.585
Acknowledge external transfers only after the copy step is complete

00:00:44.585 --> 00:00:44.735
.
